From decd7a55842e5a94498d574b4782f7d207271cf1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: handylinux <8155246+handylinux@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 07:40:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] patch 147: slot choice on catalog, drop window.prompt, fix
 hardcoded string
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three call sites moved onto the alert catalog.

Both-slots-busy now uses one catalog entry shared by regular armour
(InventoryScreen) and power armour (CharacterContext). The logic is the
same in both places: a free limb is used silently, and only when both are
taken does the app ask which to replace. On web this used to be a
window.prompt asking the player to type 1 or 2 by hand — anything else
did nothing, silently. Now three real buttons on both platforms, with the
side labels passed in as parameters (bracers for arms, greaves for legs).

CharacterScreen save error: the message was hardcoded in Russian, so an
English UI showed Russian text, and the title read tCharacterScreen('title')
— a key that does not exist, so the dialog header literally said 'title'.
Added errors.saveFailed to both locales and pointed the entry at the
existing alerts.errorTitle.

Also drops the now-unused tPAAction helper. All catalog keys verified
present in ru-RU and en-EN; no window.prompt left in the codebase.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
